Let the host protect every outbound peer socket

A VPN app on Android builds a tunnel that carries its own peer links, so a link
that is dialled while the tunnel is up goes into the tunnel unless the socket is
exempted first (VpnService.protect). Excluding the peer's address from the routes
works only for the peers known when the interface is built.

  core.SocketProtector   called with the descriptor of each outbound socket
                         before it connects; a refusal aborts the dial
  linkTCP.dialerFor      wraps its Control, which covers tcp, tls, ws, wss and
                         socks: they all dial through it
  linkQUIC.dial          quic.DialAddr opens a socket that nothing can reach, so
                         the socket is made here with a ListenConfig and handed
                         to quic.Dial; it is closed when the connection ends,
                         because a transport does not close a socket it was given

link_protect_test.go calls each transport with a counting protector, and with
one that refuses.

